          "file": "ch04-conclusion.md",
          "content": "# Chapter 4: 结语——\"现象媒介\"之意蕴\n\n## Core Idea\nThe disclosure of 现象媒介 lays a new existential-ontological foundation for media and media studies, guiding researchers to rethink the relations between media and humans, media and nature, and media and society.\n\n## Frameworks Introduced\n- **存在论转向 (Ontological Turn)**: shifting media studies from epistemology (how do we know media?) to ontology (how do media constitute being?).\n  - When to use: when designing media research that goes beyond content-effects models.\n- **媒介即生存方式**: media are not just tools but the very way humans exist in the world. A media history is a human survival history.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- **媒介学的存在论基础**: the ground that media studies has been missing — media as constitutive of human existence, not merely instruments.\n- **媒介与人/自然/社会的关系**: the three axes that the phenomenal-media framework reconfigures.\n\n## Mental Models\n- Think of media as the \"infrastructure of existence\" — like roads, but for meaning.\n- The phenomenal turn does not abolish object-media research; it re-founds it on its proper ground.\n\n## Anti-patterns\n- **在客观和科学的口号中错失理解媒介的密码**: pursuing quantitative objectivity while ignoring the subjective-perceptual constitution of the very object being measured.\n\n## Key Takeaways\n1. 现象媒介 provides a new ontological foundation for media studies.\n2. Media studies must move beyond the object/phenomenon dichotomy.\n3. The phenomenal turn reconfigures how we understand media's relations to humans, nature, and society.\n\n## Connects To\n- **Ch 1-3**: the conclusion synthesizes the foregoing analysis.\n- **彼得斯《奇云》**: a related attempt that stopped short of full phenomenological reduction.\n"
