      "skill_text": "---\nname: rui-media-phenomenology\ndescription: \"Knowledge base from 理解媒介：从对象到现象 by 芮必峰 & 孙爽. Use when applying embodied phenomenology of media, analyzing object-vs-phenomenal media distinctions, studying media as lived experience, or referencing media philosophy concepts.\"\n---\n\n# 理解媒介：从对象到现象\n**Author**: 芮必峰, 孙爽 | **Pages**: ~12 | **Chapters**: 4 | **Generated**: 2026-10-24\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\n- **Without arguments** — load core frameworks for reference\n- **With a topic** — ask about `现象媒介`, `具身化`, `意向性`, or another indexed topic; I find and read the relevant section\n- **With section** — ask for `ch03`; I load that specific section\n- **Browse** — ask \"what sections do you have?\" to see the full index\n\nWhen you ask about a topic not covered in Core Frameworks below, I will read\nthe relevant section file before answering.\n\n---\n\n## Core Frameworks & Mental Models\n\n### 对象媒介 vs 现象媒介 (Object Media vs Phenomenal Media)\n- **Use when** analyzing how media research conflates media-objects with lived media experience.\n- Object media treats media as external, measurable, objectively existing artifacts. Phenomenal media is media as it appears in lived bodily experience — \"显现在本己身体经验中的媒介\".\n- **Key insight**: 对象媒介是现象媒介的理论化产物；现象媒介先于对象媒介，是其意义根源。\n- **Anti-pattern**: Equating \"媒介\" with \"媒介物\" leads to \"万物皆媒\" which abolishes media studies itself.\n\n### 媒介的具身化 (Embodiment of Media)\n- **Use when** questioning disembodied models of communication.\n- 身体是\"元媒介\" — the most originary medium, the medium of all media. Media are extensions of the phenomenal body, not objects added to a pre-existing subject.\n- **Key insight**: \"身体是在世界上存在的媒介物\" — to have a body is to be embedded in an environment. Media originate from the body's need to overcome its limitations (distance, time, perception).\n- **Complementarity logic (斯蒂格勒)**: 外延之物恰恰在其外延过程中形成 — there is no interiority before the extension.\n\n### 现象媒介的五重特征 (Five Features of Phenomenal Media)\n1. **含混性与规范性** — media are neither pure material carriers nor pure meaning; they are the original synthesis of both. The double-negation (\"既非...也非...\") yields the double-affirmation (\"既是...又是...\").\n2. **意向性与对象性** — all consciousness is consciousness-of-something. Media inherit the body's intentional directedness toward the world. 对象媒介 is the deposit of 身体意向 into a specific object.\n3. **象征性与表达性** — media not only symbolize (refer to) reality but express (create) reality. 媒介即意义，媒介即存有.\n4. **情境性与普遍性** — media are always generated in concrete situations, yet presuppose a universal horizon of world-access. The body's \"thickness\" (厚度) is irreducible — complete transparency would abolish media.\n5. **主体性与主体间性** — media actively constitute reality (not just reflect it); intersubjectivity grounds the possibility of communication.\n\n### 现象学还原方法 (Phenomenological Reduction)\n- **Use when** need to trace a constituted object back to its constitutive lived experience.\n- Step: suspend the \"objective\" attitude → return to the lived body's original relation with the world → describe phenomena as they appear.\n- Applied here: from 对象媒介 (constituted) back to 现象媒介 (constituting).\n\n---\n\n## Section Index\n\n| # | Title | Key Frameworks |\n|---|-------|----------------|\n| [ch01](chapters/ch01-object-vs-phenomenal.md) | 对象媒介与现象媒介 | 对象/现象区分, 离身传播困境, 李普曼拟态环境批判 |\n| [ch02](chapters/ch02-embodiment.md) | 媒介的具身化 | 身体元媒介, 梅洛-庞蒂具身现象学, 补余逻辑 |\n| [ch03](chapters/ch03-five-features.md) | 现象媒介的主要特征 | 含混性, 意向性, 象征性, 情境性, 主体间性 |\n| [ch04](chapters/ch04-conclusion.md) | 结语：\"现象媒介\"之意蕴 | 存在论基础, 媒介与人/自然/社会关系 |\n\n## Topic Index\n\n- **现象媒介** → ch01, ch03\n- **对象媒介** → ch01\n- **具身化/元媒介** → ch02\n- **含混性** → ch03\n- **意向性** → ch03\n- **象征性/表达性** → ch03\n- **情境性** → ch03\n- **主体间性** → ch03\n- **身体厚度** → ch03\n- **媒介即存有** → ch03, ch04\n\n## Supporting Files\n\n- [glossary.md](glossary.md) — all key terms with definitions\n- [patterns.md](patterns.md) — all techniques and patterns\n- [cheatsheet.md](cheatsheet.md) — quick reference tables and decision guides\n\n---\n\n## Scope & Limits\n\nThis skill covers the article content only. The article is a theoretical essay in communication studies; it does not provide empirical methods or quantitative tools. For hands-on media analysis, combine with domain-specific research methods.\n"
